### =====================================================================
### Workshop request collection.
### Open in VS 2022 or VS Code (with the REST Client extension) and click
### "Send Request" above each block. Assumes the host runs on port 7218.
### =====================================================================

@base = http://localhost:7071/api
@apiKey = local-demo-key-12345

### ---- Track A: Learning ----

### S1 — the absolute minimum
GET {{base}}/S1_HelloWorld

### S2 — route param + query string
GET {{base}}/greet/Monika?loud=true

### S3 — POST body + validation (valid)
POST {{base}}/sum
Content-Type: application/json

{ "numbers": [3, 4, 5] }

### S3 — POST body (bad JSON -> 400)
POST {{base}}/sum
Content-Type: application/json

{ oops

### S4 — public (no key)
GET {{base}}/secure/public

### S4 — function-key protected (open locally; needs key in Azure)
GET {{base}}/secure/key

### S5 — dependency injection + config
GET {{base}}/di/Team

### ---- Track B: Enterprise Order Intake API ----

### Create order WITHOUT the api key -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-1

{ "customerId": "CUST-100", "currency": "USD", "lines": [ { "sku": "A1", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 9.5 } ] }

### Create order WITH key -> 201 Created
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-abc

{ "customerId": "CUST-100", "currency": "USD", "lines": [ { "sku": "A1", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 9.5 }, { "sku": "B2", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5 } ] }

### Retry the SAME Idempotency-Key -> 200 OK, same order (no duplicate)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-abc

{ "customerId": "CUST-100", "currency": "USD", "lines": [ { "sku": "A1", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 9.5 }, { "sku": "B2", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5 } ] }

### Validation failure -> 400 problem+json
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: bad-1

{ "customerId": "", "currency": "US", "lines": [] }

### List all orders
GET {{base}}/orders
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Get one (replace the id with one returned by Create)
GET {{base}}/orders/REPLACE_WITH_ID
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
